content.text:
verdict: clean
scenario_results:
  - {scenario: 1, result: pass, notes: "name, description, tools, maxTurns are lines 2-5 of frontmatter, before type/id/owner; nothing external needed to fill the seat; 'You hold the requirements seat' commits to no actor kind."}
  - {scenario: 2, result: pass, notes: "No sentence states when the role acts or what precedes/follows it; all prose is who-and-what-for."}
  - {scenario: 3, result: pass, notes: "Exactly one exclusive-domain claim, decision-phrased: 'what counts as done for a behavior is decided by this seat alone.'"}
  - {scenario: 4, result: pass, notes: "Five bullets, each an output or judgment verifiable after a run (artifacts exist, scenarios tagged/hashed/testable, answers grounded, cold-readable picture, glossary entries); no character traits."}
  - {scenario: 5, result: pass, notes: "Authoring stance matched by Write/Edit tools; maxTurns 60 caps drift; remaining stance claims ('decided by this seat alone') have no mechanical enforcement available, which the rubric permits."}
stumbles: ["stably hashed", "grounded in the requirements artifacts", "New domain vocabulary flowing to the glossary"]
top_changes: ["Define or link 'stably hashed' — a fresh reader cannot tell what makes a scenario hash stable or how to verify it", "Point 'the glossary' and 'the requirements artifacts' at their basis locations so grounding claims are checkable without tribal knowledge", "Justify Bash and Grep/Glob in tools or trim them — the stated work is authoring and answering, and unused capability widens the contract beyond the stance"]
